{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789584706,"nonce":"S4IL6I2PGJNR1nrPikgfTH7/ktQ=","message":"Commit dba30093a88a96b82044eca455711bb340d7da10 makes SSA convert nonempty Type::Tuple to the same value struct layout as lowering.rs instead of falling back to i64. A regression test constructs a growable list of (i64, f64) values, pushes a tuple, reads it, verifies a pointer-to-struct element slot, and compiles the module with Cranelift and LLVM. All 22 Python conformance categories pass with the change. This proves the compiler path for an inline tuple element; the Python frontend still boxes BODIES and PAIRS and does not yet populate typed tuple lists. The issue remains open.","files":null}]}